These folders contain testing and training data that Kavi used 
in his initial ML models for classifying cyanobacteria from other
image types. The training data is in TrIN and the Testing data is 
in Test. Note that the category names may not be fully correct. For
example, "Algie" is spelled wrong (should be Algae") and "Anabaena"
is more accurately a folder for all filamentous cyanobacteria types.
The Test folder also contains, a label list of the true image classes:
labels.csv

Kavi's models are provided on Github:
https://github.com/KaviFrancis/cyanobacteria-ovr-classifier
https://github.com/KaviFrancis/Cyanobacteria-Pseudo-Label
https://github.com/KaviFrancis/Cyanobacteria-Binary-Model-Trainer-macOS

I believe the latter is built for a macOS platform.
I belive the first and/or second were designed to be used on the Clark HPC GPUs.
